# The outcome of every template in rule2-by-type.cpp, in source order: the
# gate in scope counts findings, and a not-admitted that turned undecided
# would keep the count (it did once); outcomes.py compares these.  After
# " | ", words the reason must contain: a right outcome for a wrong reason
# fails too.
twice admitted
doubled not admitted | invalid operands
either undecided | a disjunction
applied undecided | without a result type
counted not admitted
branching undecided | if constexpr
pick undecided | resolved to another overload
pick admitted
swapped admitted
commuted not admitted | the result type Commuted asks more
thrice admitted
nested not admitted | convertible_to<T> used other than
kept not admitted
summed not admitted | narrowed
cast_sum admitted
boxed not admitted | convertible_to<T> used other than
zeros not admitted | countr_zero
listed undecided | resolved to another overload
listed admitted
moved not admitted | convertible_to<T> used other than
smaller undecided | several integer parameters
same_through admitted
twice_strict undecided | UnaryOperator
via_strict undecided | negated constraint
fresh admitted
fresh_copyable not admitted | deleted constructor
branched not admitted | convertible_to<T> used other than
compared not admitted | convertible_to<T> used other than
applied_once admitted
wide admitted
either_value admitted
halved admitted
as_int not admitted | bit_cast
